# Review ownership for Aperture.
#
# HONESTY NOTE: this project has exactly ONE maintainer identity. There is no review team,
# no per-area owner group, and no rotation — inventing one here would misrepresent who is
# actually reviewing. Every rule below therefore resolves to the same owner. The file exists
# so that ownership is explicit and so that per-area owners can be added later by editing
# rules rather than by introducing the concept.
#
# The identifier is the publishing organisation's handle, not a person. No personal names
# and no email addresses appear in this file, and none may be added — it ships publicly.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins: the global rule first, specific paths after it.
#
# ONLY PATTERNS THAT MATCH SOMETHING. A CODEOWNERS pattern matching no real path silently
# disables review for what its author thought it covered, so a stale rule is worse than a
# missing one. Patterns here are checked against the tree. Directories that do not exist yet
# — the client workspace, the contract tree, the end-to-end suite, CI configuration — are
# covered by the global rule below and get their own rules when they land, not before.

# Everything, including any path added in future.
*                       @moosenet-io

# Governance and pipeline configuration. Changing what gets published, what is protected,
# or how a vulnerability is reported is a higher-consequence edit than a feature change.
/LICENSE                @moosenet-io
/SECURITY.md            @moosenet-io
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @moosenet-io
/CODEOWNERS             @moosenet-io
/.moosenet-pipeline.yaml @moosenet-io
/.gitattributes         @moosenet-io

# The specs this repository is built from, and the reviews that shaped them.
/specs/                 @moosenet-io
/reviews/               @moosenet-io

# Documentation and repo identity.
/README.md              @moosenet-io
/behavior-spec.md       @moosenet-io
/docs/                  @moosenet-io

# Brand assets. Anything shipped to a client bundle gets the same scrutiny as code.
/assets/                @moosenet-io
